---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';

export const frontmatter = {
  title: 'Helpful advice & builder checklist | VFC Construction',
  description: 'Answers to common building questions and a printable contractor due diligence checklist.',
  ogTitle: 'Helpful advice & builder checklist | VFC Construction',
  ogDescription: 'Answers to common building questions and a printable contractor due diligence checklist.',
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={frontmatter.title}
  description={frontmatter.description}
  ogTitle={frontmatter.ogTitle}
  ogDescription={frontmatter.ogDescription}
  currentPage="faq"
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="BUILD WITH CONFIDENCE"
    title="Good questions.<br />Better decisions."
    lead="Practical starting points for planning your project and choosing a contractor you can trust."
  />

  <section class="wrap faq-layout">
    <aside>
      <h2>What would you<br />like to know?</h2>
      <label for="faq-search">Search our FAQs</label>
      <div class="search-box"><i data-lucide="search" aria-hidden="true"></i><input type="search" id="faq-search" placeholder="Try payments or planning" /></div>
      <p id="faq-count" aria-live="polite" class="caption">8 questions</p><a class="text-link" href="#checklist">Your contractor checklist ↓</a>
    </aside>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do I need planning permission?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <p>Requirements depend on the property, location and proposed work. Planning permission and building regulations approval are separate matters. Check with your local planning authority before work starts; listed buildings, conservation areas and leasehold properties may have additional requirements.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How are project payments arranged?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <p>Ask for a written stage payment schedule linked to clearly defined work. Do not pay the full contract value in advance. VFC’s payment stages and any deposit are agreed in the individual project contract.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What insurance and safety information should I request?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <p>Ask for current insurance relevant to the work, details of who will be on site, and the competence and qualifications of specialist trades. There is no single universal health and safety certificate for every building project. Agree site safety responsibilities before work begins.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do you offer a free survey?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <p>Contact Vaildo to discuss an initial consultation and feasibility survey. Availability and whether specialist reports or investigations involve a separate charge will be confirmed before booking.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Which areas do you cover?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <p>Our main service area is London and Greater London. Our company history also includes commercial work in Bristol, Newcastle, Liverpool, Birmingham, Leeds and Manchester. Contact us about work further afield.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can you help with housing association or leasehold requirements?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <p>Discuss landlord, freeholder and housing association approvals early. Their consent may be needed in addition to local authority permissions. The requirements and who handles each submission should be recorded in the project scope.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What happens if the scope changes?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <p>Ask for each change to be documented with its price and programme impact before authorising the additional work. Keep an agreed record throughout the project.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is the work guaranteed?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <p>Ask for written workmanship guarantee terms, exclusions and any relevant manufacturer warranties for your specific project. Confirm what certification will be provided at handover.</p>
      </details>
      <p id="faq-empty" hidden>No matching questions. Try a different phrase or contact us.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="pale section" id="checklist">
    <div class="wrap checklist-wrap">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">KEEP YOUR PROJECT ON SOLID GROUND</p>
        <h2>Contractor due<br />diligence checklist.</h2>
        <p>Use these prompts before you appoint a builder. Tick items as you go, then print your checklist or save it as a PDF.</p><button class="button" id="print-checklist">Print / save checklist <i data-lucide="printer" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
        <p id="check-progress" aria-live="polite">0 of 9 checked</p>
      </div>
      <div class="checklist">
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="check-0" /><span>Request relevant recent client references.</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="check-1" /><span>Check current insurance covers your proposed work.</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="check-2" /><span>Agree the scope, each stage and its target completion date.</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="check-3" /><span>List exclusions, allowances and likely additional work.</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="check-4" /><span>Record stage payments and avoid full payment upfront.</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="check-5" /><span>Confirm who is authorised to work on site and who supervises.</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="check-6" /><span>Get a written contract with start date, schedule and payment terms.</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="check-7" /><span>Verify planning permission or building regulations approval where needed.</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="check-8" /><span>Agree a defects/snagging period and final handover process.</span></label>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="wrap section advice" id="winter">
    <p class="eyebrow">PROPERTY CARE NOTES</p>
    <h2>Prepare your home<br />for the colder months.</h2>
    <div class="value-grid">
      <section>
        <h3>Windows & condensation</h3>
        <p>Condensation can have several causes. Moisture between double-glazed panes may indicate a failed sealed unit; moisture on the room side can relate to humidity and cold surfaces. Ask for an assessment before choosing repairs.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h3>Heating & lighting</h3>
        <p>Unevenly heating radiators may need maintenance. Ask a qualified technician to investigate. Consider suitable LED lighting and use heating controls according to the system guidance.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h3>Insulation & ventilation</h3>
        <p>Insulation upgrades should suit the building and its moisture conditions. Keep required ventilation clear; never seal combustion air vents. Have damp or persistent condensation assessed before covering it up.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">General project information, not a property-specific survey. Confirm permissions and technical requirements with the relevant authority and qualified professionals.</p>
    <p class="sources">Further guidance: <a href="https://www.planningportal.co.uk/permission">Planning Portal</a> · <a href="https://energysavingtrust.org.uk/advice/ventilation/">Energy Saving Trust</a> · <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/construction/areyou/domestic.htm">HSE domestic clients</a></p>
  </article>

  <section class="cta wrap">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT CHAPTER STARTS HERE</p>
      <h2>Let’s build something<br />you’re proud of.</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Tell us what you have in mind.<br />We’ll help you find the way forward.</p><a class="button" href="/contact">Request a free survey <i data-lucide="arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
